'''''Oedipodiella''''' is a [[genus]] of [[moss]] in the family [[Gigaspermaceae]]; it contains the single species '''''Oedipodiella australis'''''.  This species is restricted to wooded areas of open [[grassland]] in [[South Africa]],<ref name="Magill 1987">{{cite book | last= Magill | first= Robert E. | year= 1987 | title= Flora of Southern Africa | chapter= Gigaspermaceae | volume= 1 | issue= 2 | pages= 299–303 | chapter-url= http://www.dulwichrunners.org.uk/gba/giga.htm | archive-date= 2016-03-03 | access-date= 2008-05-18 | archive-url= https://web.archive.org/web/20160303174534/http://www.dulwichrunners.org.uk/gba/giga.htm | url-status= dead }}</ref> although a variety (''O. australis'' var. ''catalaunica'') is reported from [[Spain]].<ref name="Mueller 1985">{{cite journal| last1=Mueller | first1=Dale M. J. | last2=Rushing  |first2=Ann E. | year=1985 | title=Development of the Gemmae of ''Oedipodiella'' (Musci). I. Scanning Electron Microscopy and Growth in Culture | journal=The Bryologist | volume=88 | issue=2 | pages=69–73| doi=10.2307/3242583| jstor=3242583 }}</ref>

